WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.112
Who is this for?

2
00:00:01.112 --> 00:00:05.838
Developers build the read path, the
identity and directory engineers run it,

3
00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.088
and the security officers review it.

4
00:00:08.088 --> 00:00:11.613
Nobody needs a tenant or a
domain until the second lab.

5
00:00:11.613 --> 00:00:16.183
What it may read is short: an ordinary
domain user's read on the directory,

6
00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:19.513
two Graph permissions and
Reader on the identities.

7
00:00:19.513 --> 00:00:24.360
One choice deserves attention: listing
delegated consent grants needs the

8
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.824
broad directory read, and that's the
only reason the inventory holds it.

9
00:00:28.824 --> 00:00:31.193
Without permission to read users,

10
00:00:31.193 --> 00:00:34.970
owners come back as bare IDs,
which is all a count needs.
